# Φ_N(j,Y) as minimal polynomial of j(q^N) over ℚ(j)

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.minpoly_jqN_eq_toAdjoin` (`3868b11e-4b3e-517f-b111-3561f9579eda`),
by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `f1467e70-3d00-583b-b36a-8e71d59aa4f5`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and let `data` be a `ModularPolynomialData N`: a polynomial
$\Phi \in (\mathbb{Z}[X])[Y]$ which is monic in $Y$, whose degree in $Y$ equals $\psi(N) = \sum_{d
\mid N,\ d \text{ squarefree}} N/d$, and which satisfies $\Phi(j_q, j_{q^N}) = 0$ in the field of
Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$; here $j_q$ is the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the
rational-coefficient power series `jNumQ` (the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant), $j_{q^N}$ is
its image `jqN N` under the ring homomorphism `qExpand ℚ N` that multiplies all exponents by $N$,
and the substitution of $j_q$ into the inner variable is the homomorphism `evalAtJ`. Write
$\mathbb{Q}\langle j_q\rangle$ for the intermediate field `IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {jq}` of the
Laurent series field, and let `data.toAdjoin` $\in \mathbb{Q}\langle j_q\rangle[Y]$ be the image of
$\Phi$ under coefficientwise application of `evalAtJGen`, i.e. substitution of the generator $j_q$
for the inner variable. Assuming `PhiIrreducible data`, that is, that `data.toAdjoin` is
irreducible, the conclusion is that the minimal polynomial of $j_{q^N}$ over $\mathbb{Q}\langle
j_q\rangle$ equals `data.toAdjoin`.

This is the classical identification of the modular polynomial $\Phi_N(j, Y)$ with the minimal
polynomial of $j(q^N)$ over the field generated by $j(q)$, the input from which the degree
$[\mathbb{Q}(j, j(q^N)) : \mathbb{Q}(j)] = \psi(N)$ is read off and hence the starting point for the
function-field description of the modular curve $X_0(N)$. It is used throughout the construction of
models of $X_0(N)$, including the results on fibres and Hecke divisors in characteristic $p$.

